# `sideEffects` whitelist

`std-ui` and `std-ui-ext` use a `"sideEffects"` whitelist in `package.json`. Unlisted modules are dropped by
bundlers when nothing is imported from them, so a registration-only file silently vanishes from production builds.

When adding, moving, renaming, or deleting a file with a top-level `registerCustomAttribute(...)`,
or similar registration (UI element hooks are class-owned via `addClassHooks`, not a side effect), update that package's `sideEffects`. Entries are `dist`
paths (mirror `src`, `.ts` -> `.js`, under `./dist/esm/`).

- `std-ui`: glob `custom-attributes/**/*.custom-attribute.js`. Name new built-in bindings `*.custom-attribute.ts`,
  register inside the file, and import its `index.js` from `compile.ts`.
- `std-ui-ext`: explicit files (`custom-attributes/event.custom-attribute.js`, `custom-attributes/class-style.custom-attribute.js`). A new registering file needs a new entry.

`registerCustomAttribute` replaces any extension with the same `(sigil, name)`; that is how `std-ui-ext`'s `@*`
(modifiers) overrides std-ui's default.
